  "request": {
    "system": "You write adversarial test scenarios for compliance monitors. Each rule below has a monitor: a small state machine, assembled by another model, that tracks the evidence status of that rule for one statement an expert made on a call. You are NOT shown the monitors. You are given the rules and what a correct monitor must do, and you write scenarios stating what should happen. Code then runs each scenario through the real monitor, and any disagreement is shown to the policy owner to inspect. A separate set of scenarios written by a human reviewer is the actual acceptance gate; yours are an independent second opinion.\n\nHow evaluation works: each predicate is supported, refuted, unknown, or conflict. Under three-valued logic, \"and\" is false if any branch is false, true if all are true, otherwise indeterminate; \"or\" is true if any branch is true, false if all are false, otherwise indeterminate; \"not\" swaps true and false. Unknown and conflict both make a predicate indeterminate.\n\nWhat a correct monitor does. It starts in UNASSESSED and reacts to two events, CLAIM_EVALUATED and CONTEXT_UPDATED, in the same way:\n- guard true → state REVIEW_REQUIRED, proposing OPEN_REVIEW_TASK, plus REQUEST_ESCALATION when the rule's on_true is \"open_review_and_escalate\".\n- guard indeterminate → if the rule's on_indeterminate is \"open_context_task\": state NEEDS_CONTEXT, proposing OPEN_CONTEXT_TASK; if it is \"open_review\": state REVIEW_REQUIRED, proposing OPEN_REVIEW_TASK.\n- guard false → state NOT_TRIGGERED. This is not a clearance: a later event can move the monitor to NEEDS_CONTEXT or REVIEW_REQUIRED.\n- Once in REVIEW_REQUIRED the monitor never leaves it, whatever later events say: only a person closes review. An event it does not handle leaves the state unchanged and proposes AUDIT_ONLY.\n\nFor each rule write 5 to 8 scenarios aimed at where an assembled monitor is most likely to be wrong:\n- one predicate unknown while another is refuted (the guard is false, not indeterminate);\n- a conflict on a single predicate;\n- context arriving later that flips the result (a second step with CONTEXT_UPDATED);\n- a later evaluation that turns false after review was already required;\n- an exception inside the guard (a not(...) branch) that should prevent the rule from firing;\n- a monitor that was not triggered and then becomes triggered.\n\nEach scenario has: a name; the rule_id; a one-sentence rationale; one to three steps, each with an event and an assignment giving a state to EVERY predicate key listed for the rule (use the keys exactly as written); the final monitor state you expect; and the effects you expect the final step to propose, listing only the ones that matter to the scenario. Effects are drawn from OPEN_REVIEW_TASK, OPEN_CONTEXT_TASK, REQUEST_ESCALATION, CLOSE_CONTEXT_TASK, AUDIT_ONLY.",
    "user": "<rules>\n{\n  \"rule_id\": \"R1\",\n  \"intent\": \"Covered issuer operating results attributed to internal company sources\",\n  \"guard_in_english\": \"the statement is about the covered issuer AND the statement gives an operating figure for one company AND the expert credits an internal company source\",\n  \"predicate_keys\": [\n    \"about_covered_issuer\",\n    \"company_specific_operating_metric\",\n    \"internal_source_claimed\"\n  ],\n  \"on_true\": \"open_review\",\n  \"on_indeterminate\": \"open_context_task\"\n}\n{\n  \"rule_id\": \"R2\",\n  \"intent\": \"Expert accessed former employer's systems or documents after leaving\",\n  \"guard_in_english\": \"the expert accessed the information after their employment ended\",\n  \"predicate_keys\": [\n    \"post_employment_access\"\n  ],\n  \"on_true\": \"open_review_and_escalate\",\n  \"on_indeterminate\": \"open_context_task\"\n}\n{\n  \"rule_id\": \"R3\",\n  \"intent\": \"Unannounced corporate event at covered issuer flagged by expert as confidential\",\n  \"guard_in_english\": \"the statement is about the covered issuer AND the statement describes an unannounced corporate event AND the expert marks the information as secret or unreleased\",\n  \"predicate_keys\": [\n    \"about_covered_issuer\",\n    \"nonpublic_corporate_event\",\n    \"confidentiality_signal_present\"\n  ],\n  \"on_true\": \"open_review\",\n  \"on_indeterminate\": \"open_review\"\n}\n{\n  \"rule_id\": \"R4\",\n  \"intent\": \"Recent issuer employee discussing issuer's current-period operating results not verified as public\",\n  \"guard_in_english\": \"the expert has worked at the covered issuer in the past 12 months AND the statement is about the covered issuer AND the statement gives an operating figure for one company AND the statement covers a period the issuer has not yet reported AND NOT (the information matches a verified public source)\",\n  \"predicate_keys\": [\n    \"expert_recent_issuer_employee(months=12)\",\n  